RED on 6f3dc7c (2 failures, evidence/A5d_red.txt):
build_appmodel_research_hints emitted hints carrying subject +
evidence_refs but NO model_revision — a hint derived before newer
observations was indistinguishable from current truth.

Fix: every hint carries model_revision = int(model.revision) at
derivation time (add_hint). For traceability only — advisory_only
stays True, the 128 bound is unchanged.

Contract suite (4): every hint carries the model's revision at
derivation; ownership-hint locators resolve to REAL entities
(endpoint_id + owner_identity_ids present in the model, evidence refs
a subset of the endpoint's own refs); staleness is detectable
(derive -> apply a newer observation -> the old hint's
model_revision < model.revision); advisory_only/source/bounded-128
unchanged (proven with a 400-ownership model).

GREEN: 4/4 (evidence/A5d_green.txt); full A5 wing 26/26.
